{UTF-8}
Maximum production rate=
	35
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Saturation level of module production (stylised logistic path).
	|

Production growth rate=
	0.3
	~	1/Year
	~	Logistic growth rate of module production.
	|

Production inflection year=
	2022
	~	Year
	~	Year in which production reaches half its maximum.
	|

Production rate=
	Maximum production rate/(1+EXP(-Production growth rate*(Time-Production inflection year\
		)))
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Logistic module production P(t).
	|

Average product lifetime=
	27.66
	~	Year
	~	Mean of the Weibull lifetime (shape 5.3759, scale 30 years; IRENA regular \
		loss).
	|

Ageing chain outflow 1=
	DELAY3I(Production rate, Average product lifetime/7, 0)
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Seven cascaded third-order delays form a 21st-order delay with the mean \
		and variance of the Weibull lifetime.
	|

Ageing chain outflow 2=
	DELAY3I(Ageing chain outflow 1, Average product lifetime/7, 0)
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Seven cascaded third-order delays form a 21st-order delay with the mean \
		and variance of the Weibull lifetime.
	|

Ageing chain outflow 3=
	DELAY3I(Ageing chain outflow 2, Average product lifetime/7, 0)
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Seven cascaded third-order delays form a 21st-order delay with the mean \
		and variance of the Weibull lifetime.
	|

Ageing chain outflow 4=
	DELAY3I(Ageing chain outflow 3, Average product lifetime/7, 0)
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Seven cascaded third-order delays form a 21st-order delay with the mean \
		and variance of the Weibull lifetime.
	|

Ageing chain outflow 5=
	DELAY3I(Ageing chain outflow 4, Average product lifetime/7, 0)
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Seven cascaded third-order delays form a 21st-order delay with the mean \
		and variance of the Weibull lifetime.
	|

Ageing chain outflow 6=
	DELAY3I(Ageing chain outflow 5, Average product lifetime/7, 0)
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Seven cascaded third-order delays form a 21st-order delay with the mean \
		and variance of the Weibull lifetime.
	|

End of life flow=
	DELAY3I(Ageing chain outflow 6, Average product lifetime/7, 0)
	~	Mt/Year
	~	End-of-life flow E: modules retiring from the stock of products in use.
	|

Demand=
	Production rate
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Modules delivered to users; production is sold in the year it is made.
	|

Products in use=
	INTEG(Demand-Collection flow-Uncollected flow, 0)
	~	Mt
	~	Stock of modules in operation (installed base).
	|

Collection flow=
	Collection rate*End of life flow
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Collected end-of-life modules, c*E.
	|

Uncollected flow=
	(1-Collection rate)*End of life flow
	~	Mt/Year
	~	End-of-life modules not collected (landfill or export).
	|

Capacity adjustment time=
	4
	~	Year
	~	Time for recycling capacity to follow the required effort (tau_K).
	|

Capacity change rate=
	(Collection flow*Target process intensity-Recycling capacity)/Capacity adjustment time
	~	Mt/(Year*Year)
	~	Loop B1: capacity follows the effort needed for the collection flow at \
		target intensity.
	|

Recycling capacity=
	INTEG(Capacity change rate, 0)
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Effort capacity K: tonnes per year that can be treated at reference \
		intensity.
	|

Inventory clearance time=
	1
	~	Year
	~	Time in which recyclers aim to clear the collected inventory (tau_B).
	|

Minimum process intensity=
	0.5
	~	Dmnl
	~	Lowest process intensity under throughput pressure.
	|

Desired treatment rate=
	Collected inventory/Inventory clearance time+Collection flow
	~	Mt/Year
	~	D = L/tau_B + c*E.
	|

Process intensity=
	MIN(Target process intensity, MAX(Minimum process intensity, ZIDZ(Recycling capacity\
		, Desired treatment rate)))
	~	Dmnl
	~	Achieved treatment effort per tonne (x). Loop B2: under throughput \
		pressure recyclers lower intensity to raise throughput.
	|

Treatment rate=
	MIN(Desired treatment rate, ZIDZ(Recycling capacity, Process intensity))
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Modules treated per year: min(D, K/x).
	|

Collected inventory=
	INTEG(Collection flow-Treatment rate, 0)
	~	Mt
	~	Collected modules awaiting treatment (L in the paper).
	|

Scenario=
	3
	~	Dmnl
	~	1 = S1 Low, 2 = S2 Medium, 3 = S3 High, 4 = S4 Near-closed.
	|

Final collection rate=
	IF THEN ELSE(Scenario=1, 0.3, IF THEN ELSE(Scenario=2, 0.6, IF THEN ELSE(Scenario=3,\
		 0.85, 0.95)))
	~	Dmnl
	~	Collection rate reached at the policy completion year.
	|

Final process intensity=
	IF THEN ELSE(Scenario=1, 0.6, IF THEN ELSE(Scenario=4, 1.6, 1))
	~	Dmnl
	~	Process intensity target reached at the policy completion year.
	|

Deep recovery switch=
	IF THEN ELSE(Scenario>=3, 1, 0)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Scenario choice: 1 = deep recovery of silicon and copper (FRELP thermal \
		and chemical steps), 0 = bulk recovery only.
	|

Initial collection rate=
	0.1
	~	Dmnl
	~	Collection rate at the policy start year.
	|

Initial process intensity=
	0.5
	~	Dmnl
	~	Process intensity target at the policy start year.
	|

Policy start year=
	2025
	~	Year
	~	Start of the linear phase-in of the circularity levers.
	|

Policy completion year=
	2040
	~	Year
	~	End of the phase-in.
	|

Policy implementation fraction=
	MIN(1, MAX(0, (Time-Policy start year)/(Policy completion year-Policy start year)))
	~	Dmnl
	~	Share of the lever change implemented, from 0 at the start year to 1 at \
		the completion year.
	|

Collection rate=
	Initial collection rate+(Final collection rate-Initial collection rate)*Policy implementation fraction
	~	Dmnl
	~	Share of the end-of-life flow that is collected (c).
	|

Target process intensity=
	Initial process intensity+(Final process intensity-Initial process intensity)*Policy implementation fraction
	~	Dmnl
	~	Target treatment effort per tonne relative to the reference process.
	|

Deep recovery status=
	Deep recovery switch*STEP(1, Policy start year)
	~	Dmnl
	~	1 when deep recovery is in operation (from the policy start year in S3 and \
		S4).
	|

Glass mass fraction=
	0.7
	~	Dmnl
	~	Mass fraction in the module (Latunussa et al. 2016).
	|

Reference recovery yield glass=
	0.98
	~	Dmnl
	~	Recovery yield of the reference process.
	|

Recovery yield glass=
	(1-(1-Reference recovery yield glass)^Process intensity)
	~	Dmnl
	~	First-order recovery: y = 1-(1-yref)^x.
	|

Recovered glass=
	Treatment rate*Glass mass fraction*Recovery yield glass
	~	Mt/Year
	~		|

Glass input requirement=
	Production rate*Glass mass fraction
	~	Mt/Year
	~		|

Secondary glass input=
	MIN(Recovered glass, Maximum cullet share*Glass input requirement)
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Closed-loop input to module production.
	|

Aluminium mass fraction=
	0.1853
	~	Dmnl
	~	Mass fraction in the module (Latunussa et al. 2016).
	|

Reference recovery yield aluminium=
	0.986
	~	Dmnl
	~	Recovery yield of the reference process.
	|

Recovery yield aluminium=
	(1-(1-Reference recovery yield aluminium)^Process intensity)
	~	Dmnl
	~	First-order recovery: y = 1-(1-yref)^x.
	|

Recovered aluminium=
	Treatment rate*Aluminium mass fraction*Recovery yield aluminium
	~	Mt/Year
	~		|

Aluminium input requirement=
	Production rate*Aluminium mass fraction
	~	Mt/Year
	~		|

Secondary aluminium input=
	MIN(Recovered aluminium, Aluminium input requirement)
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Closed-loop input to module production.
	|

Silicon mass fraction=
	0.0365
	~	Dmnl
	~	Mass fraction in the module (Latunussa et al. 2016).
	|

Reference recovery yield silicon=
	0.95
	~	Dmnl
	~	Recovery yield of the reference process.
	|

Recovery yield silicon=
	(1-(1-Reference recovery yield silicon)^Process intensity)*Deep recovery status
	~	Dmnl
	~	First-order recovery: y = 1-(1-yref)^x.
	|

Recovered silicon=
	Treatment rate*Silicon mass fraction*Recovery yield silicon
	~	Mt/Year
	~		|

Silicon input requirement=
	Production rate*Silicon mass fraction
	~	Mt/Year
	~		|

Secondary silicon input=
	MIN(Recovered silicon, Silicon input requirement)
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Closed-loop input to module production.
	|

Copper mass fraction=
	0.0046
	~	Dmnl
	~	Mass fraction in the module (Latunussa et al. 2016).
	|

Reference recovery yield copper=
	0.95
	~	Dmnl
	~	Recovery yield of the reference process.
	|

Recovery yield copper=
	(1-(1-Reference recovery yield copper)^Process intensity)*Deep recovery status
	~	Dmnl
	~	First-order recovery: y = 1-(1-yref)^x.
	|

Recovered copper=
	Treatment rate*Copper mass fraction*Recovery yield copper
	~	Mt/Year
	~		|

Copper input requirement=
	Production rate*Copper mass fraction
	~	Mt/Year
	~		|

Secondary copper input=
	MIN(Recovered copper, Copper input requirement)
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Closed-loop input to module production.
	|

Maximum cullet share=
	0.3
	~	Dmnl
	~	Ceiling on cullet in the glass batch (assumption).
	|

Glass to open loop recycling=
	Recovered glass-Secondary glass input
	~	Mt/Year
	~	Recovered glass above the cullet limit, used outside module production.
	|

Recycled content share=
	ZIDZ(Secondary glass input+Secondary aluminium input+Secondary silicon input+Secondary copper input\
		, Glass input requirement+Aluminium input requirement+Silicon input requirement+Copper input requirement\
		)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Secondary share of the four-material input to module production.
	|

Primary emission factor glass=
	1.1
	~	tCO2e/t
	~		|

Reprocessing emission factor glass=
	0.5
	~	tCO2e/t
	~	Emissions of bringing the recovered fraction to production grade.
	|

Net emission saving glass=
	Primary emission factor glass-Reprocessing emission factor glass
	~	tCO2e/t
	~		|

Primary emission factor aluminium=
	15.1
	~	tCO2e/t
	~		|

Reprocessing emission factor aluminium=
	0.52
	~	tCO2e/t
	~	Emissions of bringing the recovered fraction to production grade.
	|

Net emission saving aluminium=
	Primary emission factor aluminium-Reprocessing emission factor aluminium
	~	tCO2e/t
	~		|

Primary emission factor silicon=
	42
	~	tCO2e/t
	~		|

Reprocessing emission factor silicon=
	31.7
	~	tCO2e/t
	~	Emissions of bringing the recovered fraction to production grade.
	|

Net emission saving silicon=
	Primary emission factor silicon-Reprocessing emission factor silicon
	~	tCO2e/t
	~		|

Primary emission factor copper=
	4.6
	~	tCO2e/t
	~		|

Reprocessing emission factor copper=
	1.8
	~	tCO2e/t
	~	Emissions of bringing the recovered fraction to production grade.
	|

Net emission saving copper=
	Primary emission factor copper-Reprocessing emission factor copper
	~	tCO2e/t
	~		|

Open loop emission credit glass=
	0.31
	~	tCO2e/t
	~		|

Reference transport emissions=
	107
	~	kgCO2e/t
	~	Transport emissions of the reference process (FRELP).
	|

Local haul share=
	0.2
	~	Dmnl
	~	Share of transport emissions that does not grow with the collection rate \
		(lambda).
	|

Reference collection rate=
	0.5
	~	Dmnl
	~	Collection rate of the reference process (c_ref).
	|

Transport emissions=
	Reference transport emissions*(Local haul share+(1-Local haul share)*(Collection rate\
		/Reference collection rate)^0.5)
	~	kgCO2e/t
	~	Collection transport emissions per tonne (b_T); mean haul grows with the \
		square root of the collection rate.
	|

Bulk separation emissions=
	48
	~	kgCO2e/t
	~	Mechanical separation of frame and glass (FRELP), scales with x.
	|

Cell layer incineration emissions=
	126
	~	kgCO2e/t
	~	Incineration of the cell layer in deep recovery (FRELP), independent of x.
	|

Chemical recovery emissions=
	89
	~	kgCO2e/t
	~	Chemical recovery of silicon and copper in deep recovery (FRELP), scales \
		with x.
	|

Separation emissions=
	Bulk separation emissions*Process intensity+Deep recovery status*(Cell layer incineration emissions\
		+Chemical recovery emissions*Process intensity)
	~	kgCO2e/t
	~	Separation and treatment emissions per tonne treated (b_S).
	|

Unit conversion kg per t=
	1000
	~	kgCO2e/tCO2e
	~	Converts kg CO2e to t CO2e.
	|

Collection and treatment emissions=
	Treatment rate*(Transport emissions+Separation emissions)/Unit conversion kg per t
	~	MtCO2e/Year
	~	Emissions of collection transport, separation and treatment.
	|

Expected benefit per tonne=
	Glass mass fraction*Primary emission factor glass+Aluminium mass fraction*Primary emission factor aluminium\
		+Silicon mass fraction*Primary emission factor silicon+Copper mass fraction*Primary emission factor copper
	~	tCO2e/t
	~	Displacement of primary production at original grade.
	|

Expected benefit=
	Treatment rate*Expected benefit per tonne
	~	MtCO2e/Year
	~	B_exp: displacement of primary production at original grade.
	|

Emission credit glass=
	Secondary glass input*Net emission saving glass+Glass to open loop recycling*Open loop emission credit glass
	~	MtCO2e/Year
	~		|

Emission credit aluminium=
	Recovered aluminium*Net emission saving aluminium
	~	MtCO2e/Year
	~		|

Emission credit silicon=
	Recovered silicon*Net emission saving silicon
	~	MtCO2e/Year
	~		|

Emission credit copper=
	Recovered copper*Net emission saving copper
	~	MtCO2e/Year
	~		|

Actual benefit=
	Emission credit glass+Emission credit aluminium+Emission credit silicon+Emission credit copper\
		-Collection and treatment emissions
	~	MtCO2e/Year
	~	B_act: emission credits minus collection and treatment emissions.
	|

CMR=
	1-ZIDZ(Actual benefit, Expected benefit)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Circular manufacturing rebound.
	|

Reprocessing emissions=
	Recovered glass*Reprocessing emission factor glass+Recovered aluminium*Reprocessing emission factor aluminium\
		+Recovered silicon*Reprocessing emission factor silicon+Recovered copper*Reprocessing emission factor copper
	~	MtCO2e/Year
	~	Emissions of bringing all recovered material to production grade.
	|

CMR grade component=
	ZIDZ(Reprocessing emissions, Expected benefit)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Layer 1: reprocessing to grade (substitution correction).
	|

CMR loop component=
	CMR-CMR grade component
	~	Dmnl
	~	Layer 2: unrecovered material, separation, transport and loop saturation.
	|

Accounting period=
	PULSE(2025, 36)
	~	Dmnl
	~	1 from 2025 to 2060, 0 otherwise.
	|

Expected benefit inflow=
	Expected benefit*Accounting period
	~	MtCO2e/Year
	~	Expected benefit counted in the accounting period.
	|

Actual benefit inflow=
	Actual benefit*Accounting period
	~	MtCO2e/Year
	~	Actual benefit counted in the accounting period.
	|

Cumulative expected benefit=
	INTEG(Expected benefit inflow, 0)
	~	MtCO2e
	~		|

Cumulative actual benefit=
	INTEG(Actual benefit inflow, 0)
	~	MtCO2e
	~		|

Cumulative CMR=
	1-ZIDZ(Cumulative actual benefit, Cumulative expected benefit)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Rebound over the accounting period 2025-2060.
	|

********************************************************
	.Control
********************************************************~
		Simulation Control Parameters
	|

FINAL TIME  = 2070
	~	Year
	~	The final time for the simulation.
	|

INITIAL TIME  = 2000
	~	Year
	~	The initial time for the simulation.
	|

SAVEPER  = 1
	~	Year [0,?]
	~	The frequency with which output is stored.
	|

TIME STEP  = 0.125
	~	Year [0,?]
	~	The time step for the simulation.
	|

